#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/breakdown.rst:3
msgid "Where each figure comes from"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/breakdown.rst:5
msgid ""
"A percentage is an answer to \"how much\"; this is the answer to "
"\"which\". Each measurement already carries the detail it was computed "
"from — coverage per file, lint findings per rule, docstrings per object —"
" and this page lays it out worst first, which is the order somebody "
"fixing it would work in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/breakdown.rst:9
msgid ""
"**Only the worst few lines of each metric appear here.** The crate alone "
"breaks down into more than a hundred files, and a page listing every one "
"of them changes in every commit that moves any of them: a committed file "
"whose diff nobody can read is a committed file nobody reads. The complete"
" detail is one command away and is never truncated:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/breakdown.rst:18
msgid ""
"How many lines a document shows is a setting, in the three tiers "
"everything else here uses — ``--breakdown-limit N``, then "
"``FREEPORTS_CI_BREAKDOWN_LIMIT``, then ``report.breakdown_limit`` in "
"``ci.yaml``, then fifteen. ``0`` means all of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/breakdown.rst:24
msgid ""
"A breakdown line is not a target. A file at 0 % may be a thin wrapper "
"around code that is thoroughly tested elsewhere, and a lint rule with "
"forty hits may be one pattern used forty times on purpose. The list says "
"where to look, not what to change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/breakdown.rst:31
msgid "**Where each figure comes from**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/breakdown.rst:33
msgid ""
"The detail each measurement already carries, worst first: the files that "
"pull a coverage figure down, and the rules a lint score is spent on. A "
"line with nothing to answer for — a document that does have a whole-"
"document test — is not listed at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/breakdown.rst:35
msgid ""
"12 metrics, 12 gated: 5 pass, 1 not measured, 6 measured at another "
"commit; branch dev → dev (thresholds are reported, not enforced); ci-"
"check: inconclusive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dev/ci-report/breakdown.rst:37
msgid ""
"*Generated by `freeports-dev ci-report`, and demonstrative: it shows what"
" one run measured on one machine, not that the software is correct. To be"
" sure of any line, re-run the command that measures it and `freeports-dev"
" ci-check` yourself.* :ref:`What is gated here, and what refuses: the "
"commit gate <commit-gate>`."
msgstr ""

